      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Steam comes in four grades. The hotter the source, the denser the steam it can make from water:\n\n- §bSteam§r - 100 mB from 1 mB of water.\n- §bDense Steam§r - 10 mB from 1 mB of water.\n- §bSuper Dense Steam§r - 1 mB from 1 mB of water.\n- §bUltra Dense Steam§r - 1 mB from 10 mB of water, and only from very hot sources.\n\nA turbine only takes steam down §eone grade§r: Steam becomes Low-Pressure Steam, Dense Steam becomes Steam, and so on, with every 1 mB of denser steam turning into 10 mB of the next grade. Chain turbines one after another to use all of the energy in dense steam - or let a single turbine take the first step and send the rest to a second one.\n\nBoilers are set to a grade with a fluid identifier. RBMK steam channels and the Fusion Boiler make the denser grades.",
